        "the square, abandoned houses on stilts stand in the water: dark board walls, black empty windows, roofs of mossy "
        "blue-grey shingles or old red-brown tiles, stone chimneys (a few still trailing smoke), ladders, barrels and hanging "
        "weed. The water here is wider and more open than in town, rippled, with drifts of green mist over it, lily pads, and "
        "broken pilings sticking out of it. The only warm light is the two lanterns at the square's near corners. The green "
